if you are a longtime watcher of this  channel you know i am a fan of  everything elon however i haven't talked  much about his boring company in a while  but now i finally have some big news to  share with you guys so stick around as i  take you through this big update and  what it might mean for subterranean  transport going forward what's the  boring company if you're unfamiliar with  the boring company you'd be forgiven for  it but unlike tesla and spacex not a lot  of people know about this venture of  elon's anyways as the name suggests the  boring company does precisely that and  no it doesn't bore people but rather it  bores through the earth making gigantic  tunnels for transportation you see elon  believes that tunneling is the solution  to the traffic log jams that most cities  face he believes that the next evolution  of terrestrial transportation will occur  underground through massive subterranean  networks of tunnels zigzagging under our  cityscapes and the boring company has  been working towards that goal since  2016 to achieve traffic-free roads in  busy areas of cities so that people can  save time fuel and money so what is this  big update that the boring company  announced recently in late april the  company announced that it had raised  another  675 million dollars in a series c  funding round which now takes its  valuation to a staggering  5.675 billion dollars but has the boring  company achieved anything to reach such  a high valuation do they even have a  working service or a proof of concept  that can be rolled out to the public to  know the answer to these questions stick  around until the end it's going to be  quite a joyride what has the boring  company achieved so far the boring  company started out with some lofty  ambitions as you would expect no doubt  from a company owned by elon but in its  5 odd years of operation the  expectations have dampened a bit don't  get me wrong even though the company is  still in its early days it has made some  significant progress but the initial  promises are taking longer than expected  to materialize the initial buzz around  the company was because of its goal to  develop the infrastructure for a  hyperloop system that can transport  people at a mind-boggling speed of 600  plus miles per hour in autonomous  electric pods although the company has  conducted various tests hyperloop still  remains a concept and a working  prototype is still years away so the  company has had to adjust its goals  towards more viable projects it has now  pivoted from hyperloops to self-driven  teslas in tunnels the only project it's  completed so far is the las vegas  convention center loop or lvcc loop it  is a three-station transportation system  consisting of 1.7 miles of tunnel built  to transport people between the  different convention halls the loop  became operational in april of 2021 and  it was the company's first proof of  concept with tesla's driving through  tunnels for now the loop is a service  provided by human-driven teslas  traveling at most 40 miles per hour  although it falls way short of the  company's earlier visions of  self-driving cars traveling as fast as  150 miles per hour moving to and from  surface streets and automated elevators  it still improves on the previous  transportation picture by some order of  magnitude the loop connects the lvcc's  west hall with the existing campus and  reduces a 45-minute cross-campus journey  time to approximately two minutes during  busy convention times it can transport  anywhere between 15 000 to 25 000  passengers per day the project took a  year to complete at the cost of  approximately 47 million dollars so  although the project is far away from  its final vision of fully self-driven  teslas ferrying people at high speeds it  was good enough for the las vegas  authorities to not only approve an  extension project to the nearby worlds  resort but on october 20th 2021 the  clark county commissioners unanimously  approved a new project called the vegas  loop a 29-mile tunnel network connecting  51 stations across the las vegas strip  this has been a major scoop for elon and  the boring company as it is the first  sign of support from a major city to  commit to its underground transportation  concept after this municipalities like  los angeles chicago and washington dc  have all started to show an active  interest in similar concepts for their  cities this has finally opened the  company's floodgates prompting renewed  interest from investors and leading to  one of this video's main focuses a fresh  round of funding what's next for the  boring company now that the company has  raised a fresh round of funding it is  looking to accelerate its tunneling  plans it is also working on developing  new technologies to reduce the cost and  time of building these tunnels according  to their recent statements most of the  new funding will be used towards its  vegas loop project still a significant  portion of the budget will also go into  developing their next generation boring  machine called the proofrock for its  first research tunnel project the boring  company basically bought a secondhand  tunnel boring machine called the godot  and modified it for their purposes after  completing this initial mile-long tunnel  the company again purchased and modified  a second machine this second generation  boring machine was called the line storm  and would serve as the company's  workhorse for the lvcc loop but all of  this tinkering of secondhand boring  machines was leading up towards  something more significant the team back  at base was working hard to develop a  unique all-electric high-powered tunnel  boring machine that could mine 10 times  faster than any existing tunneling  machine the proofrock according to elon  existing tunnel boring companies spend  only about 10 minutes per hour actually  drilling the other 50 minutes are spent  installing the reinforcements removing  all the dirt and deploying all the  logistics behind the mining process this  makes existing tunneling technology  extraordinarily inefficient and costly  with proofrock the boring company is  working to increase the overall  efficiency of tunneling by a factor of  three they have modified the cutter  design and added an automated segment  erection system by engineering a system  that automatically takes care of all the  reinforcement and dirt removal the  company predicts a 15 times improvement  in the speed of boring versus the next  best technology out there proofrock 1  first broke ground in early 2020 with  the company commemorating that moment  with a tweet proofrock is alive since  then the new boring machine has been  hard at work expanding the lvcc loop and  now it will be used exclusively for the  29 miles of the las vegas loop as it  drills this new network of tunnels the  company will continuously improve the  design and release new versions of the  proofrock along the way what about the  hyperloop although the company is  focused on optimizing its tesla driven  tunnel transportation concept it hasn't  forgotten about the ultimate goal the  hyperloop right after securing this new  round of funding in late april the  company tweeted hyperloop testing at  full scale begins later this year elon  also chimed in by tweeting that the  boring company will attempt to build a  working hyperloop in the coming years  although he was strangely non-committal  about a time frame when probed further  by twitter users i believe despite the  boring company attempting to drum up  interest in the hyperloop once again the  project is far from being realized that  doesn't mean the company is not working  on it it most definitely has a team  researching it in earnest still for now  i believe the company will be laser  focused on achieving its lesser dream of  having autonomous tesla zigzagging  underground at speeds of 150 miles an  hour first after all it needs a fully  operational public mode of transport  that generates revenue to justify its  enormous valuation to its investors if  you think about it the sooner the  company completes the las vegas loop and  makes it operational the better it will  be for its reputation and credibility as  there are many people out there who are  critically looking at the company for  boasting such an enormous valuation  without having developed a single  revenue generating service and in the  future if the company can successfully  pair fast autonomous teslas with quick  tunnelling technology then many more  city councils across the us will be  interested in allowing them to tunnel  their streets and have super quick  point-to-point transportation so because  of all the reasons mentioned above i  believe the hyperloop will take a bit of  a back seat for now but who knows it is  a company backed by elon after all and  we all know how quickly they can bring  about technological breakthroughs so  maybe we will get to see a working  hyperloop before this decade runs out  what do you think do you agree with my  prediction let me know in the comment  section below if you enjoyed this update  on the boring company give this video a  like and subscribe to the channel see  you in the next one

